{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION (re-opened, unaddressed): budget accounting undercounts the envelope by ~28 chars**

`used = heading.length + 4` assumes the envelope costs 4 chars, but the actual envelope is `<system-notice>` (14) + `\n` + `</system-notice>` (16) + the newline after the heading ≈ heading + 32; each line's `+1` covers its own separator, so the block can render ~28 chars over `maxChars`. Harmless at 6000, but it will silently distort the ≤1%-of-window budget when the window-coupled wiring lands. The budget test deliberately pins only eviction order (derived from the full render), so this arithmetic is uncovered — worth one assertion that `renderObligationsBlock(ledger, maxChars: b).length <= b` for a closed-only ledger.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment5.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION (re-opened, unaddressed): synthetic-content entries get a fresh random id on every parse**

`ObligationEntry.fromJson` mints `uuidv7()` when `id` is missing. Tolerant-parse goals (E6) are met, but the minted id is never stable: an id-less entry parsed at rehydration — and at every projection — carries a different id per process, so the future `obligation_mark_done` tool can never address it by id, and two parses of the same payload produce different round-trip payloads (`toPayload()` after `fromPayload()` ≠ input — the round-trip test only covers fully-populated entries). Consider a deterministic fallback (e.g. a hash of `sourceRecordId + kind + text`) or document that id-less entries are read-only.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment6.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION (new): the CLI glue has no test coverage — and a windowed-residency test would have caught the blocking issue**

The new wiring in this file — the E3 engine gate, the lazy writer rehydration/swap (`_obligationsWriterFor`), the swallow-on-append-failure policy, and the steering/timestamp path through `_persistIncremental` — ships with zero tests. The strong new suite (`obligations_ledger_test.dart`, 17 tests) exercises the library and the `Session` projection seam, but never `AgentCli`. Since ingest keys on record ids and the writer's cumulative state is cached per session object, the failure modes here are silent and permanent:

- a regression in the gate or the writer swap silently stops classification for the rest of the session;
- a rehydration regression is exactly the windowed data-loss bug in the other thread — a test that opens the session **windowed** (`_repo.open(metadata, windowed: true)`), slides the snapshot out of residency, appends a classified message, and asserts the pre-boundary entries survive would have caught it before review.

Suggested: one test group driving `AgentCli` (or at least `_ingestObligations`/`_obligationsWriterFor` against a windowed `JsonlSessionRepo`): classification lands, append-failure swallows, session switch rebuilds the writer, windowed resume neither loses the block nor erases entries.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment7.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION (new): both classic branches now scan `getEntries()` redundantly — pass `entries:` like the structured branch does**

`_withObligationsBlock` accepts an optional `entries` list precisely so the caller can reuse its scan (the structured branch does: `entries: entries`). The two classic branches don't:

- line 525 branch: `RecordSeqIndex(await getEntries())` immediately followed by `_withObligationsBlock(...)` without `entries` → a second full list copy + scan per context build;
- line 520 branch (no classic hidden): previously made **zero** `getEntries()` calls; now makes one per build.

On the degenerate full-open path (marathon resume fallback, `session_commands.dart:576`) that list is the whole file. Cheap fix: hoist `final entries = await getEntries();` once at the top of `_projectMessages`, build `RecordSeqIndex(entries)` from it, and pass `entries: entries` in all three `_withObligationsBlock` call sites.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment8.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION (new): hardcode-recorded type string — use the exported `obligationsLedgerRecordType` constant**

This registration site (and `trajectory_snapshot_builder.dart:39` in `hiddenCustomRecordTypes`) repeats the literal `'obligations_ledger'` instead of using the `obligationsLedgerRecordType` constant exported by `lib/src/session/obligations_ledger.dart`. The constant exists, is barrel-exported, and importing it creates no cycle (`obligations_ledger.dart` is a leaf importing only `session_record`/`types`/`uuid`). Three independent spellings of the wire-format string is one rename away from a silently divergent repair/trajectory registration — single-source it:

